cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this paper or its computations, please cite it as below.
  Please also cite the OpenAI preprints listed in UPSTREAM.md.
type: software
title: 'Hamiltonian fixed points below the stable Morse number in dimension ten'
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-10-09'
authors:
  - name: '[AUTHOR NAME]'
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A simply connected closed Kahler manifold of real dimension 10 with a
  nondegenerate Hamiltonian diffeomorphism having lambda(M) - 4 fixed points,
  fewer than the stable Morse number; the count equals the Bai-Xu cyclic
  integral Floer bound. No counterexample exists in real dimension 6, and in
  dimension 8 no finite-order element of a Hamiltonian torus action can
  produce one after perturbation. The results were found and checked by
  Claude (Anthropic) agents under the repository owner's direction. No human
  peer review has taken place and nothing is formalized in Lean; no
  historical-priority claim is made.
keywords:
  - Arnold conjecture
  - stable Morse number
  - Hamiltonian fixed points
  - Artin-Mumford threefold
  - Floer homology
references:
